ProtocolFeeCollector::harvest
├── given PAUSE_TYPE is paused
│   └── it should revert with IsPaused
└── given PAUSE_TYPE is not paused
    ├── when sourceTypes and sources lengths do not match
    │   └── it should revert with ProtocolFeeCollectorLengthMismatch
    ├── when both arrays are empty
    │   └── it should complete without emitting Harvested or HarvestingFailed
    ├── when the source type is BORROW_MARKET
    │   ├── given source is not a registered borrow market
    │   │   ├── it should emit HarvestingFailed
    │   │   └── it should not emit Harvested
    │   ├── given source borrow token is not DUSD
    │   │   ├── it should emit HarvestingFailed
    │   │   └── it should not emit Harvested
    │   ├── given source is paused for PAUSE_TYPE
    │   │   ├── it should emit HarvestingFailed without accruing or withdrawing
    │   │   └── it should not emit Harvested
    │   ├── given source fee recipient is not the collector
    │   │   ├── and the collector has zero supply shares
    │   │   │   ├── it should emit HarvestingFailed after accrual
    │   │   │   └── it should not emit Harvested or call removeSupply
    │   │   └── and the collector has existing supply shares
    │   │       └── it should still withdraw the collector's existing position
    │   └── given source is a registered unpaused DUSD borrow market
    │       ├── it should accrue market interest before reading the collector position
    │       ├── it should harvest fee shares created for the collector during accrual
    │       ├── when the collector has zero supply shares and is the fee recipient
    │       │   ├── it should not call removeSupply
    │       │   └── it should emit Harvested with zero DUSD received
    │       ├── when the collector supply shares convert to zero assets
    │       │   ├── it should not call removeSupply
    │       │   └── it should emit Harvested with zero DUSD received
    │       ├── when the market has zero available liquidity
    │       │   ├── it should not call removeSupply
    │       │   └── it should emit Harvested with zero DUSD received
    │       ├── when the market DUSD balance is below its accounting liquidity
    │       │   └── it should cap available liquidity to the market DUSD balance
    │       ├── when claimable assets are less than or equal to available liquidity
    │       │   ├── it should remove the collector's full supply share balance
    │       │   ├── it should send the withdrawn DUSD to the collector
    │       │   └── it should emit Harvested with the collector's DUSD balance increase
    │       └── when claimable assets are greater than available liquidity
    │           ├── it should remove only the available DUSD assets
    │           ├── it should send the withdrawn DUSD to the collector
    │           └── it should emit Harvested with the collector's DUSD balance increase
    ├── when the source type is MINT_MARKET
    │   ├── given source is not a registered mint market
    │   │   ├── it should emit HarvestingFailed
    │   │   └── it should not emit Harvested
    │   ├── given source borrow token is not DUSD
    │   │   ├── it should emit HarvestingFailed
    │   │   └── it should not emit Harvested
    │   ├── given source fee recipient is not the collector
    │   │   ├── it should emit HarvestingFailed without claiming fees
    │   │   └── it should not emit Harvested
    │   ├── given source is paused for PAUSE_TYPE
    │   │   ├── it should emit HarvestingFailed without accruing or claiming
    │   │   └── it should not emit Harvested
    │   └── given source is a registered unpaused DUSD mint market with the collector as fee recipient
    │       ├── it should accrue market interest before claiming fees
    │       ├── it should call claimInterest with zero to claim all fees
    │       └── it should emit Harvested with the collector's DUSD balance increase
    ├── when the source type is VAULT
    │   ├── given the vault registry is not configured
    │   │   └── it should emit HarvestingFailed and skip the source
    │   ├── given source is not a registered vault
    │   │   └── it should emit HarvestingFailed and skip the source
    │   ├── given source asset is not DUSD
    │   │   └── it should emit HarvestingFailed and skip the source
    │   ├── given source fee recipient is not the collector
    │   │   ├── when the collector has zero shares
    │   │   │   └── it should emit HarvestingFailed and skip the source
    │   │   └── when the collector has residual shares
    │   │       └── it should redeem the existing position without realizing new fee shares
    │   └── given source is a registered DUSD vault
    │       ├── when the collector has zero shares and is the fee recipient
    │       │   ├── it should use zero-share redemption to run the fee-accrual path
    │       │   └── it should emit Harvested with zero DUSD received when no fees accrue
    │       ├── when source is a real AltoVault with zero collector shares
    │       │   └── it should complete the zero-share accrual path and emit Harvested with zero DUSD received
    │       ├── when performance-fee shares are pending
    │       │   ├── it should realize the pending shares before reading maxRedeem
    │       │   └── it should redeem the realized shares into DUSD
    │       ├── when maxRedeem is zero
    │       │   ├── it should retain all collector shares
    │       │   └── it should emit Harvested with zero DUSD received
    │       ├── when maxRedeem equals the collector share balance
    │       │   └── it should redeem all collector shares into DUSD
    │       ├── when maxRedeem is below the collector share balance
    │       │   ├── it should redeem only maxRedeem
    │       │   └── it should retain the residual shares for a later harvest
    │       └── when a vault interaction reverts
    │           ├── it should emit HarvestingFailed and retain the collector shares
    │           └── it should continue harvesting later sources
    ├── when the source type is USM
    │   ├── given source is not a registered USM
    │   │   ├── it should emit HarvestingFailed
    │   │   └── it should not emit Harvested
    │   ├── given source stable token is not DUSD
    │   │   ├── it should emit HarvestingFailed
    │   │   └── it should not emit Harvested
    │   ├── given source fee recipient is not the collector
    │   │   ├── it should emit HarvestingFailed without distributing fees
    │   │   └── it should not emit Harvested
    │   └── given source is a registered DUSD USM with the collector as fee recipient
    │       ├── it should call distributeFeesToFeeRecipient
    │       ├── it should emit Harvested with the collector's DUSD balance increase
    │       ├── when swaps are frozen, it should still distribute fees and emit Harvested
    │       └── when the USM is seized, it should still call fee distribution and emit Harvested
    ├── when the source type is FLASH_MINTER
    │   ├── given source is not the configured flash minter
    │   │   ├── it should emit HarvestingFailed
    │   │   └── it should not emit Harvested
    │   ├── given source DUSD token is not the configured DUSD
    │   │   ├── it should emit HarvestingFailed
    │   │   └── it should not emit Harvested
    │   ├── given source fee recipient is not the collector
    │   │   ├── it should emit HarvestingFailed without distributing fees
    │   │   └── it should not emit Harvested
    │   └── given source is the configured DUSD flash minter with the collector as fee recipient
    │       ├── it should call distributeFeesToFeeRecipient
    │       └── it should emit Harvested with the collector's DUSD balance increase
    ├── when calldata contains a source type outside the FeeSourceType enum
    │   └── it should revert without data during ABI decoding before entering harvest
    ├── when source validation or execution reverts
    │   ├── it should emit HarvestingFailed without emitting Harvested
    │   ├── it should roll back that source's earlier state changes
    │   └── it should allow retrying the source after the failure is resolved
    ├── when harvestSource is called from outside the collector
    │   └── it should revert with ProtocolFeeCollectorUnauthorized
    └── when multiple sources are provided
        ├── it should process each source in array order
        ├── it should preserve earlier harvests and continue after validation or execution failure
        ├── it should emit Harvested once for each successful source
        ├── it should emit HarvestingFailed once for each invalid source
        └── it should be callable by any address
